From 81815b7dc5eb88471f59291694a76ec71320babd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: klave7 <5594473+klave7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:13:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Blurred bars around the picture
 image

New iOS setting "Bars around the picture" (DM_BAR_FILL): Black, Blurred picture
(default) or Still image. A screen that is not 16:9 shows the game's picture
with bars; they now show a dimmed, blurred copy of the picture or
bar_background.jpg instead of black. The picture is never stretched or cropped.

The fill is drawn in the Metal 4 present pass (present_encode_m4, nvn_mtl.m), so
it applies to every game, NVN or Vulkan: the picture's valid rectangle is drawn
into a small texture, blurred along x and y, and drawn dimmed over the whole
canvas before the sharp picture. It also works through MetalFX (the scaled
picture is what is blurred). A screenshot's present keeps black bars. The game
view is the whole screen while a fill is on, and the touch mapping follows the
picture as the present drew it (mtl_present_aspect).

bar_background.jpg is an image generated with Gemini by the repository's author.

Tested on an iPhone Duo with Super Mario Galaxy, closed and open, Standard and
MetalFX upscaling; not tested on other devices or games.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
